# What never reaches the build context.
#
# This file does real work rather than tidying, because backend/Dockerfile builds
# from the REPOSITORY ROOT -- it has to, so that store-config.json is reachable
# (see the comment at the top of that file). Without these rules the daemon would
# receive the entire repo, node_modules and .venv included.
#
# Docker reads .dockerignore only from the context root, so this belongs here and
# not in backend/.

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The one that actually matters. An image with .env baked in hands its Stripe
# secret key and database password to anyone who can pull it -- and a pushed
# image is far harder to un-share than a file. .env.example stays out too; it is
# documentation, useless inside a container.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- weight ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 166 MB, and Linux-incompatible anyway: a venv hardcodes absolute paths and
# links against the host's interpreter. If one leaked in it would not work, it
# would just make the image enormous.
backend/.venv/

# The web app is deployed separately to Amplify (task 8). None of it belongs in
# the API image, and node_modules is the single largest directory in the repo.
web/
**/node_modules/

# --- code the production image has no use for --------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md's rule is about DEPENDENCIES -- the image installs requirements.txt
# alone, so pytest is absent. This excludes the test FILES as well. The two fail
# independently, which is why both are verified separately.
backend/tests/

# --- noise -------------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
docs/
infra/
mobile-android/
mobile-ios/
*.md
.claude/
